until a certain message.

00:38:39.390 --> 00:38:42.420
And the new pipeline takes
on at the next message.

00:38:42.420 --> 00:38:45.990
You've not actually lost any
message in the process, right?

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:48.030
You can replace a
running pipeline

00:38:48.030 --> 00:38:49.740
with no transformation.

00:38:49.740 --> 00:38:53.470
And the other thing, we kind of
glossed over it a little bit,

00:38:53.470 --> 00:38:57.260
but as the Dataflow pipeline
was writing things out,

00:38:57.260 --> 00:38:59.310
it was writing
them into BigQuery.

00:38:59.310 --> 00:39:03.090
And we could be querying the
data, even as it was done.

00:39:03.090 --> 00:39:05.010
You saw the Firebase app.

00:39:05.010 --> 00:39:08.760
The Firebase app was making
a query into BigQuery,

00:39:08.760 --> 00:39:13.030
even as the data
were streaming in.

00:39:13.030 --> 00:39:14.890
Again, we made it
look very easy, right?

00:39:14.890 --> 00:39:17.050
But this is extremely,
extremely hard.

00:39:17.050 --> 00:39:21.660
Think about being able to do
querying on streaming data,

00:39:21.660 --> 00:39:22.160
right?

00:39:22.160 --> 00:39:24.160
And we're doing SQL
queries on streaming data

00:39:24.160 --> 00:39:27.040
to power that Firebase
graphical thing

00:39:27.040 --> 00:39:30.250
and, finally, to be
able to do your training

00:39:30.250 --> 00:39:32.470
on your machine learning model.

00:39:32.470 --> 00:39:35.620
And the good thing
is that all of this

00:39:35.620 --> 00:39:38.230
will auto-scale to thousands
of machines on demand.

00:39:38.230 --> 00:39:40.610
All we are writing is
we are writing code.

00:39:40.610 --> 00:39:41.530
We're writing code.

00:39:41.530 --> 00:39:43.030
We are defining the logic.

00:39:43.030 --> 00:39:46.470
And everything else
is just auto-scaling.

00:39:46.470 --> 00:39:50.380
The other thing that we
took a huge advantage of

00:39:50.380 --> 00:39:53.290
was that when Alex
did his training,

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:56.570
he was training
it on batch data.

00:39:56.570 --> 00:39:59.380
But then when we
did the predictions,

00:39:59.380 --> 00:40:03.880
we were predicting
on streaming data.

00:40:03.880 --> 00:40:07.340
And it was actually a
very easy transition.

00:40:07.340 --> 00:40:10.190
And the only reason that it
was a very easy transition

00:40:10.190 --> 00:40:13.250
was that Reza was
using Dataflow.

00:40:13.250 --> 00:40:15.410
And Dataflow is a
programming model

00:40:15.410 --> 00:40:18.530
that lets you deal with
batch data and streaming data

00:40:18.530 --> 00:40:20.250
in exactly the same way.

00:40:20.250 --> 00:40:22.610
So we could train a
model on historical data,

00:40:22.610 --> 00:40:24.350
which is what you always do.

00:40:24.350 --> 00:40:27.800
But you predict on
newly arriving data,

00:40:27.800 --> 00:40:31.570
which is what you always want.

00:40:31.570 --> 00:40:36.520
And we didn't get into this,
but the model that Alex built,

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:38.320
that was his first model.

00:40:38.320 --> 00:40:41.080
And over time we'll need to
do hyper-parameter tuning.

00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:42.880
We'll need to tune the models.

00:40:42.880 --> 00:40:45.670
And all of that
is also automatic.

00:40:45.670 --> 00:40:50.280
All of these things about tuning
a model and making them better,

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:54.940
those can also be all part of
your whole process of making

00:40:54.940 --> 00:40:56.500
them completely automatic.

00:40:56.500 --> 00:41:04.810
So bottom line, then, what
GCP offers to data scientists,

00:41:04.810 --> 00:41:07.690
to data engineers
is that we offer

00:41:07.690 --> 00:41:09.970
a way to fuel your innovation.

00:41:09.970 --> 00:41:11.440
You write your innovation.

00:41:11.440 --> 00:41:13.390
We give you the rocket ship.

00:41:13.390 --> 00:41:16.780
We give you the rocket ship
to fuel your innovation.

00:41:16.780 --> 00:41:19.030
Whether you're talking
about ingestion with PubSub,

00:41:19.030 --> 00:41:21.520
you're talking about
transformation with Dataflow,

00:41:21.520 --> 00:41:25.030
you're talking about analyzing
a data with BigQuery,

00:41:25.030 --> 00:41:27.430
doing your experimentation
with Datalab,

00:41:27.430 --> 00:41:29.770
you're doing machine
learning with Cloud ML,

00:41:29.770 --> 00:41:31.660
it all just works.

00:41:31.660 --> 00:41:36.870
And that's ultimately the
thing that makes it all--

00:41:36.870 --> 00:41:39.100
it's all very well integrated.

00:41:39.100 --> 00:41:42.680
And it provides you a
huge amount of innovation.

